          "evidence": "The statement permits m=1; the scalar variational equation is step 2.1 and the commuting-flow implication is step 5.1."
        },
        {
          "case": "degenerate",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "At zero time the flow is identity and J(0,q)=I by step 2.1."
        },
        {
          "case": "endpoints",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "All flow identities are restricted to times for which the local maps remain in the neighborhood, as stated and used in steps 3.2, 4.1, and 5.1."
        },
        {
          "case": "nonempty-choice",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "The linear variational and second-variation equations use uniquely determined contraction solutions in steps 2.1 and 3.1; no choice principle is used."
        },
        {
